    <section class="rise-fall" id="timeline" aria-labelledby="timeline-title">
      <h2 class="profile-section-title" id="timeline-title">Timeline</h2>
      <ol class="rf-events"><li><span class="rf-year">c. 610</span><span class="rf-text">Muhammad receives his first revelation in the cave of Hira near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a>, according to Islamic tradition</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">622</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hijra">Hijra</a>: Muhammad and his followers migrate from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medina">Medina</a>, the start of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islamic-calendar">Islamic calendar</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">632</span><span class="rf-text">Muhammad dies in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medina">Medina</a>; Abu Bakr becomes the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">c. 650</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> Uthman has the text of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quran">Quran</a> gathered and copies sent to the main cities</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">680</span><span class="rf-text">Husayn, Muhammad’s grandson, is killed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-karbala">Karbala</a>, an event central to Shia Islam</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">691–692</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dome-of-the-rock">Dome of the Rock</a> is completed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">711</span><span class="rf-text">Muslim armies cross from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a> into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1924</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/republic-of-turkey">Republic of Turkey</a> abolishes the Ottoman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphate</a></span></li></ol>
